  "title": "Terraced Watershed Republics",
  "rules": [
    "All 384 residents move and act separately. Tools distinguish workers, couriers, engineers, growers and guards and can be exchanged.",
    "Sluices send at most canal capacity 1 or 2 per tick. Water traverses three native transit slots and arrives on a later step.",
    "An engineer can divert new parcels east; parcels already traveling retain their original destination.",
    "Top terraces receive rain every eight ticks. Reservoirs store more water; walls tolerate overflow and protect flooded roads.",
    "Growers spend local water to irrigate and local provisions to plant. Growth requires moisture and time; floods damage crops.",
    "Guards grant a nearby foreign crew entry while in their own territory. Revoking entry blocks future crossings, not motion within an occupied region.",
    "Couriers physically load provisions at home and deliver them abroad; entry permissions and flood roads constrain travel.",
    "This world ends at the finite evaluation horizon. Native scenes and fixed scripts are authored and have not been executed."
  ],
